{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's own chat message asked the driver to stop at IMM first, and the driver agreed. Under POL-RD-04 the deviation is exonerated to the extent it is attributable to that rider instruction, so the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor must be excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0]",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's instruction satisfies POL-RD-04(a) to (c): it came from the rider (MSG-02856-001, sender RIDER), it was timestamped 2026-09-14T15:33:19+08:00, within three minutes of the trip starting at 15:32:19, and it named a specific place, IMM, with a resolved waypoint_hint at lat 1.3348, lng 103.7466. The driver acknowledged it ('ok') at 15:33:34.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02856", "EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].sent_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The gps_trace does not corroborate the rider's IMM instruction: the nearest fix to the IMM waypoint was 3088.34 m away, far outside the 200 m threshold set by POL-RD-04. Under POL-RD-14 the instruction did not cause the measured excess, POL-RD-04 does not apply, no distance is excluded, and the deviation is decided under POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 on the trace as measured. This is not the contradiction POL-RD-10(7) describes, because a request that was made and a route that did not follow it are consistent with each other.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02856", "EV-CHAT-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-14", "POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's assertion of an external traffic cause carries no weight. The bundle holds no traffic_advisory covering the trip window: EV-ADVIS-02856-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0, so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and under POL-RD-08 the driver's uncited traffic assertion does not discharge his burden. Under POL-RD-13 the missing advisory is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation because the driver cited no advisory identifier.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02856-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.advisories",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on this trip's own trace. The gps_trace records trace_distance_km of 23.79 km against an optimal_distance_km of 18.3 km, an excess of 5.49 km or 30.0%. That exceeds both POL-RD-01 establishment tests: greater than 20% of optimal (3.66 km) and greater than 0.8 km absolute. The trace figure governs over the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km of 23.8 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02856", "EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The excess of 5.49 km is not a MATERIAL deviation: it is below both the 50% of optimal (9.15 km) and the 8.0 km absolute materiality thresholds in POL-RD-01, so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not triggered and no repeat-deviation pattern can be established. The driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 and completed_trips_90d is 408, far below the 3-flag or 0.05-ratio tests.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02856", "EV-GPS-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and has discharged it: the trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip_id TRP-02856 and the pickup timestamp 2026-09-14T15:32:19+08:00 matches across the trace and trip record, and the excess of 5.49 km meets the POL-RD-01 threshold on an unimpaired trace. The burden shifts to the driver, who has pointed to no specific artifact and clause that exonerates the excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02856", "EV-GPS-02856", "EV-FARE-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The gps_trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: it has 100.0% coverage, 187 fixes at a 10 s sample interval, zero gaps and a max_gap_sec of 0.0, so none of limbs (a) to (c) fire. The deviation may therefore be established on the trace alone and no independent corroboration is required.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs. The recomputed fare on the booked optimal route is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 18.3 + 0.28 x 24.7) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP = 25.2410. The refund is charged_total 31.13 less 25.2410 = 5.8890, rounded up to SGD 5.90. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share, so a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 5.90 is the arithmetic outcome.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02856", "EV-TRIP-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No ERP or surcharge correction is due. The fare_breakdown carries zero ERP gantries and zero tolls, and no airport surcharge line, so there is no off-route or phantom pass-through line to refund under POL-RD-09 and nothing to add on top of the POL-RD-02 figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile does not trigger the POL-RD-08 corroboration requirement: deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the threshold of 4, so no additional corroboration beyond the gps_trace is required for this claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02856"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.9,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider: your route-deviation complaint succeeds in part. Driver: you are not exonerated. The trip from Blk 12 Telok Blangah Cres to Blk 130 Bukit Batok West Ave 6 is measured at 23.79 km on the GPS trace against a booked optimal route of 18.3 km — an excess of 5.49 km, or 30.0% of optimal (EV-GPS-02856, EV-TRIP-02856). Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests are met (more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km absolute), so the deviation is established on this trip's own trace. The trace figure governs over the rounded 23.8 km trip-record copy. The excess is below both materiality gates (50% of optimal, or 8.0 km), so this is a deviation but not a MATERIAL one. | Driver, your answer is that the rider asked for IMM. That instruction is real: MSG-02856-001, sent by the rider at 15:33:19 — one minute after the meter started — and you replied 'ok' at 15:33:34. POL-RD-04 exonerates only where the trace corroborates the instruction, and POL-RD-14 governs where it does not. The platform's waypoint analysis puts the nearest fix to the IMM hint (1.3348, 103.7466) 3,088.34 m away, and within_threshold is false. The request was made and the route did not follow it, which is a failed corroboration, not the balanced contradiction POL-RD-10(7) describes. No distance is excluded; the deviation stands on the trace as measured. Your counterparty statement — that the rider asked for IMM — is accepted so far as it goes, but it does not show the detour was actually driven, and the rider's own account is the opposite: you never went to IMM. | The fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs arithmetically. Charged total: $31.13. Recomputed fare on the optimal route: (($3.80 + $0.75 x 18.3 km + $0.28 x 24.7 min) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + $0.80 platform fee + $0 ERP = $25.2410 (EV-FARE-02856). Refund = $31.13 - $25.2410 = $5.8890, rounded up to $5.90. That is above the $0.50 de minimis floor and well below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of $5.90. | No ERP, toll or surcharge correction is due under POL-RD-09: the fare breakdown carries zero gantries, zero tolls and no airport surcharge line, so there is nothing to add on top of the POL-RD-02 figure and no phantom line to refund. No billing-integrity referral follows. | No traffic advisory was on file for this trip: EV-ADVIS-02856-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. No party cited an advisory identifier as an exculpatory record, so under POL-RD-13 the gap is a bundle gap, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation; POL-RD-03 is simply unavailable and no traffic cause reduces the excess or supplies an amended optimal. | The GPS trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 187 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires — identifiers and pickup timestamps agree across the trip record, trace and fare breakdown; the trace is clean; the refund is far below the $150 ceiling and below charged_total; and there are no unexplained charge lines. | The driver's profile shows no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 408 completed trips in 90 days), so POL-RD-06 neither uplifts the remedy nor makes a conduct referral; the excess is not MATERIAL in any event. The rider's profile does not trigger the POL-RD-08 corroboration requirement (deviation_claims_60d 1). No driver compensation arises under POL-RD-04: the billed distance (23.8 km) is not more than 1.0 km short of the trace distance (23.79 km). | Confidence is 0.9, capped by the deciding artifacts, all at weight_multiplier 1.0; the only impaired artifact is the absent advisory, which carries no deciding fact. The monetary effect of $5.90 is at or below the $8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so it executes on issue, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The trace is clean for policy purposes and no escalation trigger fires. The gps_trace has 187 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps and a max gap of 0 s, so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) are not met and the trace is not impaired. The trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, the timestamps run forward, the refund of 5.90 is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling and below charged_total, and the only missing artifact is the advisory, which no party cited as an exculpatory record and which is therefore a gap in the bundle rather than a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction. The case is decidable and should be ruled, not escalated.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02856-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The driver's assertion of an external traffic cause carries no weight. The bundle holds no traffic_advisory covering the trip window: EV-ADVIS-02856-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0, so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and under POL-RD-08 the driver's uncited traffic assertion does not discharge his burden. Under POL-RD-13 the missing advisory is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation because the driver cited no advisory identifier.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02856-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
